        <mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
    Six-year clean streak
  </h2>
</mj-text>

<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Dubai has retained its title as the <a href="https://www.khaleejtimes.com/uae/dubai-worlds-cleanest-city-6-years-in-a-row" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #102341; color: black;">world's cleanest city</a> for the sixth straight year, scoring 100% in the Global Power City Index's cleanliness indicator. The recognition highlights Dubai Municipality's round-the-clock operations, with 785 vehicles, 23,300 waste units, and initiatives such as the Warsan Waste-to-Energy Centre and Circle Dubai, aligning with the 2041 waste management strategy for a circular economy.</p>
</mj-text>

<mj-divider
  border-style="dashed"
  border-width="1px"
  border-color="lightgrey"
  padding="0px 12px 4px 12px"
/>

<mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
    Fairmont Palm operational
  </h2>
</mj-text>

<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Fairmont The Palm <a href="https://www.khaleejtimes.com/business/fairmont-palm-remains-fully-operational-after-debris-fall-incident" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #102341; color: black;">remains fully operational</a> after drone debris from Iranian attacks fell on February 28, causing limited car park damage and injuring four individuals nearby. No hotel guests or staff were harmed; a small fire was quickly contained with the aid of Civil Defence. Executives confirmed all safety protocols remain active amid flexible booking policies for affected regional guests.</p>
</mj-text>

<mj-divider
  border-style="dashed"
  border-width="1px"
  border-color="lightgrey"
  padding="0px 12px 4px 12px"
/>

<mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
    Emergency alert noise
  </h2>
</mj-text>

<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">The UAE has changed how its national emergency phone alerts sound <a href="https://gulfnews.com/uae/your-safety-alert-will-sound-a-bit-different-says-uaes-ncema-1.500469004" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #102341; color: black;">depending</a> on the time of day. From 9am to 10:30pm, alerts use the current high-tone alarm, ending with a standard message tone. From 10:30pm to 9am, both the alert and its end use a standard text tone.</p>
</mj-text>
